tip1=Low memory slows everything down. Closing unused tabs and apps keeps Windows from leaning on your disk.
tip2=An up-to-date graphics driver means sharper video, smoother games and fewer flickers or freezes.
tip3=Switching from a hard drive to an SSD is usually the biggest speed upgrade for an older PC.
tip4=Dust clogs fans and makes a PC hot and slow. Clean the vents every 6-12 months.
tip5=Unexpected shutdowns can point to a failing power supply, battery or overheating - worth checking early.
tip6=Restarting at least once a week clears memory and fixes many odd glitches, even with Fast Startup on.
tip7=A dead pixel is a dot that never changes colour. Check early - warranties often cover only the first weeks.
tip8=Slow internet isn't always your provider. Try a LAN cable, move closer to the router, or switch DNS.
tip9=Keep at least 10% of drive C: free so Windows Update and your apps can work properly.
tip10=On laptops, keeping the battery between 20% and 80% helps it last longer.
